---
// Every number here comes from benchmarks/graph-tools-comparison/results.json,
// one run of a harness whose raw responses are published beside it. The three
// passes agreed to the token on four of the six arms; the two that moved are
// named in the caveat rather than smoothed away.
const arms = [
  {
    name: "kivgraph",
    version: "0.3.6",
    tokens: "6,381",
    precision: "0.94",
    exact: "6/7",
    index: "52.0 s",
    ours: true,
  },
  {
    name: "graphify",
    version: "0.8.31",
    tokens: "2,469",
    precision: "0.54",
    exact: "1/7",
    index: "11.7 s",
  },
  {
    name: "graft",
    version: "0.10.1",
    tokens: "9,027",
    precision: "0.14",
    exact: "1/7",
    index: "26.4 s",
  },
  {
    name: "codebase-memory-mcp",
    version: "0.8.1",
    tokens: "26,439",
    precision: "0.67",
    exact: "4/7",
    index: "5.1 s",
  },
  {
    name: "code-review-graph",
    version: "2.3.7",
    tokens: "109,298",
    precision: "0.67",
    exact: "3/7",
    index: "7.7 s",
  },
  {
    name: "grep + reading",
    version: "—",
    tokens: "63,531",
    precision: "1.00",
    exact: "7/7",
    index: "—",
    baseline: true,
  },
];

const findings = [
  "A name is not a symbol. `withRetry` is declared seven times in this corpus, in three languages, and three of the five resolve callers by name: one drags four TypeScript files into a Go answer, one attributes another package's tests to this declaration, and one drops the cross-file callers and says it may undercount.",
  "`grep` plus reading answers all seven. It is the honest denominator, and none of the five matches it — ours included. What the graph buys is nearly the same answer for a tenth of the tokens, not a better one.",
  "We are the slowest to index and the heaviest on disk, and the only one that needs a toolchain. That row is in the table on purpose.",
];
---

<div class="space-y-10">
  <p class="max-w-[68ch] text-sm text-gray-300">
    Five tools that call themselves code graphs, asked the same seven questions
    over the same 37-repository monorepo, against a manual ground truth. Plus a
    sixth arm: <code>grep</code> and reading the files, which is what an agent
    already has.
  </p>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-xs">
      <caption class="sr-only">
        Tokens, precision and exact answers for five code-graph tools and for
        grep, over seven questions
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-rule-strong text-left text-gray-400">
          <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-6">tool</th>
          <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap">tokens</th>
          <th scope="col" class="py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap">exact</th>
          <th scope="col" class="hidden py-2 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap sm:table-cell"
            >precision</th
          >
          <th scope="col" class="hidden py-2 whitespace-nowrap md:table-cell"
            >cold index</th
          >
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          arms.map((arm) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-rule align-baseline">
              <td class="py-3 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap">
                <span class={arm.ours === true ? "text-accent-200" : "text-gray-300"}>
                  {arm.name}
                </span>
                <span class="ml-2 text-gray-500">{arm.version}</span>
              </td>
              <td
                class={
                  arm.baseline === true
                    ? "py-3 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap text-gray-500"
                    : "py-3 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap text-gray-300"
                }
              >
                {arm.tokens}
              </td>
              <td
                class={
                  arm.ours === true
                    ? "py-3 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap text-graph-exact"
                    : "py-3 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap text-gray-400"
                }
              >
                {arm.exact}
              </td>
              <td class="hidden py-3 pr-6 whitespace-nowrap text-gray-300 sm:table-cell">
                {arm.precision}
              </td>
              <td class="hidden py-3 whitespace-nowrap text-gray-400 md:table-cell">
                {arm.index}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <ol class="space-y-5">
    {
      findings.map((finding, index) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-rule pt-5 text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span class="shrink-0 text-graph-exact" aria-hidden="true">
            {`0${index + 1}`}
          </span>
          <span set:html={finding.replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>')} />
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="max-w-[68ch] text-xs text-gray-500">
    One machine, one corpus, seven questions, three passes. Four of the six arms
    returned the same number every pass; code-review-graph moved by 0.1% and
    codebase-memory-mcp by 1.8% and between three and four exact answers. Only
    the free, model-free tiers were measured. The harness, the ground truth and
    every raw response are published, and so is the longer version with the
    losses in full: <a
      class="text-accent-200 underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-200"
      href="/comparison/">the full comparison</a
    >.
  </p>
</div>
